.TH PARROT-JANITOR 1 "13 October 2026" "parrot-janitor 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
parrot-janitor \- system janitor GUI for Parrot OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B parrot-janitor
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B parrot-janitor
is a Qt6 desktop utility for Parrot OS that bundles together jobs that htop,
KDE System Monitor and bleachbit do not do on their own: runaway process
detection, resource monitoring, port exposure analysis, Docker lab
management, btrfs snapshot management and disk cleanup.
.PP
All privileged operations are performed through
.B pkexec
(polkit), so the desktop's graphical authentication prompt is used instead of
a bare
.BR sudo .
.SH TABS
.TP
.B Processes
Live CPU/RAM table. A process becomes
.I HOT
once its CPU reaches the threshold (default 90%) and
.I RUNAWAY
once it has stayed there for the sustain period (default 60s). Both are
adjustable. The binary path and owning Debian package are resolved in the
background. Kill sends SIGTERM behind a confirmation dialog.
.TP
.B Resources
Per-thread utilisation bars, a rolling 7-minute CPU/RAM history chart, load
average, memory split into in-use / reclaimable cache / free, swap usage and
temperatures from /sys/class/thermal.
.TP
.B Ports & exposure
Every listening socket from
.BR ss (8),
classified by scope (loopback / LAN / multicast / all interfaces), then
checked with a real TLS handshake or a protocol banner read. Verdicts are
.BR Secured ,
.BR Local ,
.BR Open ,
.BR Exposed
and
.BR Unknown .
A connect-test of 36 well-known ports gives an explicit open/closed answer.
A read-only view of
.BR ufw (8)
and
.BR nft (8)
rules is available behind polkit.
.TP
.B Docker
Container list with live CPU/memory and bulk start/stop/restart.
.TP
.B Snapshots
Create, inspect and delete read-only btrfs snapshots of
.I @
and
.I @home
under
.IR /.
snapshots/.
.TP
.B Disk
Size overview, big-file finder, empty trash, purge pip cache and delete a
selected cache entry, each behind a confirmation dialog.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the argument summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-smoke
Run a headless self-check: sample processes, query Docker, exercise the
helper functions and construct every widget, then exit non-zero if anything
is broken. No window is displayed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/parrot-janitor/parrotjanitor.py
The application itself.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/parrot-janitor.desktop
Application menu entry.
.TP
.I /usr/share/icons/hicolor/*/apps/parrot-janitor.*
Application icon.
